    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0861" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.001W69/2.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-05T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1913—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. Your March 4, conveying a message to the President from General Felix Díaz.
                    The President desires you to say orally to General Díaz that his message is
                    highly appreciated, that his good wishes are reciprocated, and that he hopes the
                    restoration of peace and prosperity throughout Mexico will soon be brought
                    about.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
